      "description": "Watch Gornik Zabrze vs Monaco highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The atmosphere was electric for this European clash as both sides looked to make their mark on the competition. Held on August 20, 2026 , the UEFA Conference League encounter between Gornik Zabrze and Monaco promised high-octane action from the opening whistle. Visitors Strike Early Monaco wasted little time establishing their authority on Polish soil. Just nine minutes into the match, the visitors took the lead when Mika Biereth found the back of the net, clinical in his finish following a well-placed assist from Mathys Detourbet . The early breakthrough allowed the principality club to dictate the tempo for much of the first half. While Gornik Zabrze attempted to find a rhythm, the physical nature of the game saw Mathys Detourbet pick up a yellow card in the 38th minute, reflecting the rising tension as halftime approached. A Whirlwind Second Half The match exploded into life after the restart with a flurry of goals that kept the fans on the edge of their seats. Lamine Camara doubled Monaco's lead in the 51st minute, but the hosts responded almost instantly. In the 53rd minute, Erik Prekop pulled one back for Gornik Zabrze after being set up by Erik Janza . The momentum swung again just five minutes later when Paris Brunner restored the two-goal cushion for the visitors, converting a chance created by Stanis Idumbo . The rapid exchange of goals showcased the offensive quality on display from both teams. Late Drama and Resilience Refusing to back down, Gornik Zabrze continued to push for a way back into the game. Their persistence paid off in the 74th minute when substitute Sondre Liseth scored, assisted by Paulo Bernardo , to make it 2-3. The closing stages were a test of nerves, characterized by tactical substitutions and defensive grit. Despite a late yellow card for Erik Janza in stoppage time as frustration grew, Monaco held firm against the home side's late onslaught to secure a hard-fought victory on the road."
